{"jobPostingInfo": {"id": "ea8e4640766310009cfb8fdfb5140000", "title": "Supplier Quality Engineer", "jobDescription": "Work Model: This is a fully onsite role, with work performed at your designated Regal Rexnord office.<br /><p>____________________</p><br /><p>Job Title:            Supplier Quality Engineer</p><p>Location:            Mumbai, India</p><p></p><p><b><u>SUMMARY</u></b></p><p>This position will be responsible for Parts Quality and Supplier Process Development, to ensure RFT and long-term process capability of outsourced parts. This position needs to work as a bridge between Portescap and suppliers.</p><p></p><p><b><u>Essential Duties and Responsibilities</u></b></p><p>Here are your key responsibilities:</p><ul><li><p>Review and assess supplier processes.</p></li><li><p>Identify quality issues.</p></li><li><p>Maintain documentation and reports.</p></li><li><p>Provide technical guidance and assistance.</p></li><li><p>Communicate with suppliers and senior management.</p></li><li><p>Ensure that products / processes supplied are managed in accordance with all specified product quality requirements and ensuring that timely and accurate information is made available to all affected parties.</p></li><li><p>Visit suppliers on a proactive &amp; regular basis to report performance and review systems and perform on-site supplier process audits for all high impact suppliers.</p></li><li><p>Coordinate for deviation requests and ensure proper approvals and tracking of material under deviation.</p></li><li><p>Manage supplier corrective actions and timely 8D closures, ensuring a thorough root cause analysis is performed, to eliminate possible recurrence of defects.</p></li><li><p>Maintain supplier records in accordance with documented requirements &amp; track supplier performance in accordance with defined guidelines.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Co-ordinate with suppliers to identify Root causes by 5 Why analysis &amp; Counter measures, also understand Supplier yield progress.</p></li><li><p>Establish optimum supplier’s product / process efficiency and quality.</p></li><li><p>Manage supplier corrective actions and ensuring thorough root cause analysis is being performed to eliminate possible reoccurrence (Verification at the supplier sites should be considered for significant concerns)</p></li><li><p>Conduct detailed supplier APQP reviews using cross-functional teams for all outsourced products prior to approving PPAP.</p></li><li><p>Review supplier manufacturing processes, collaborate with suppliers on process improvement and value enhancement opportunities.</p></li><li><p>Support the Quality Manager to monitor and report on supplier product quality and performance.</p></li><li><p>Ensure compliance to RoHS, REACH and Conflict Minerals statutory requirements.</p></li><li><p>Participate in cross-functional teams in the development of new products or changes related to current products in meeting customer requirements.</p></li><li><p>Manage and coordinate supplier Parts Per Million (PPM), supplier problem solving on time, cost recovery and supplier warranty indicators.</p></li><li><p>Lead quality audits.</p></li><li><p>Support and lead process improvement activities at the supplier.</p></li><li><p>Undertake special projects as required.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to continuous improvement activities.</p></li><li><p>Facilitate the escalation of unresolved supplier quality issues within assigned projects and suppliers.</p></li><li><p>Execute, monitor, review and improve supplier score card on regular basis.</p></li><li><p></p></li></ul><p><b>Education and Experience Requirements</b></p><ul><li><p>Diploma (with Exp. of 10&#43; Yrs.) / BE (with experience of 7&#43; Yrs.)</p></li></ul><p></p><p><b>Functional Competencies</b></p><ul><li><p>Strong know-how of Machining, Stampings, Plastics and Electronics parts (knowledge of different commodities e.g., sheet metal, machining, adhesives, molding etc.)</p></li><li><p>Hands-on experience in part validation (PPAP) and Quality tools</p></li><li><p>Strong expertise in Process Development at Supplier</p></li><li><p>Ensure compliance to RoHS, REACH and Conflict Minerals statutory requirements.</p></li><li><p>Exposure to Kaizen and Lean Manufacturing techniques</p></li><li><p>Working proficiency in usage of MS-Office Tools (Excel, Word &amp; PowerPoint)</p></li><li><p>Understand Engineering drawings and documents.</p></li><li><p>Well conversant with implementing standards &amp; Quality Systems like DIN, ISO, TS16949, OSHAS   </p></li><li><p>Working knowledge of ERP (Oracle / SAP etc.)       </p></li></ul><p></p><h2><u>KEY RELATIONSHIPS:</u></h2><p><b><u>Internal</u></b>: Incoming Quality &amp; QA, Production, Engineering, Sourcing, Purchase &amp; Stores</p><p><b><u>External</u></b><b>: </b>Suppliers</p><h1></h1><p><u>LANGUAGE SKILLS:</u></p><p>Fluency in Verbal and written communication English &amp; Hindi</p><br /><h1><b><u>About Regal Rexnord</u></b></h1><br /><p>Regal Rexnord is a publicly held global industrial manufacturer with 30,000 associates around the world who help create a better tomorrow by providing sustainable solutions that power, transmit and control motion. The Company’s electric motors and air moving subsystems provide the power to create motion. A portfolio of highly engineered power transmission components and subsystems efficiently transmits motion to power industrial applications. The Company’s automation offering, comprised of controls, actuators, drives, and precision motors, controls motion in applications ranging from factory automation to precision control in surgical tools.</p><br /><p>The Company’s end markets benefit from meaningful secular demand tailwinds, and include factory automation, food &amp; beverage, aerospace, medical, data center, warehouse, alternative energy, residential and commercial buildings, general industrial, construction, metals and mining, and agriculture.</p><br /><p>Regal Rexnord is comprised of three operating segments: Industrial Powertrain Solutions, Power Efficiency Solutions, and Automation &amp; Motion Control. Regal Rexnord has offices and manufacturing, sales and service facilities worldwide. For more information, including a copy of our Sustainability Report, visit RegalRexnord.com.</p><br /><br /><p><b>Notification to Agencies</b>: Please note that Regal Rexnord Corporation and its affiliates and subsidiaries (&#34;Regal Rexnord&#34;) do not accept unsolicited resumes or calls from third-party recruiters or employment agencies. In the absence of a signed Master Service Agreement or similar contract and approval from HR to submit resumes for a specific requisition, Regal Rexnord will not consider or approve payment to any third-parties for hires made.</p>", "location": "Mumbai, Maharashtra, India", "postedOn": "Posted 30+ Days Ago", "startDate": "2026-08-31", "timeType": "Full time", "jobReqId": "R26_04359", "jobPostingId": "Supplier-Quality-Engineer_R26_04359", "jobPostingSiteId": "Careers", "country": {"descriptor": "India", "id": "c4f78be1a8f14da0ab49ce1162348a5e"}, "logoImage": {"src": "/wday/cxs/regalrexnord/Careers/sidebarimage/c5e3da43d73d1013009d9bae04f90000", "alt": "logo"}, "canApply": true, "posted": true, "includeResumeParsing": true, "jobRequisitionLocation": {"descriptor": "Mumbai, Maharashtra, India", "country": {"descriptor": "India", "id": "c4f78be1a8f14da0ab49ce1162348a5e", "alpha2Code": "IN"}}, "remoteType": "On-site", "externalUrl": "https://regalrexnord.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Mumbai-Maharashtra-India/Supplier-Quality-Engineer_R26_04359", "questionnaireId": "9f2c34dba2a01000a8f1f0fe0ddd0000", "timeLeftToApply": "30+ days left to apply", "endDate": "2026-12-31", "jobPostingEndDateAsText": "End Date: December 31, 2026"}}